export anchor AthleticNeonStyle:
    number: 384
    screen: FitnessTracker
    name: Athletic neon
    idea: A sports poster in volt yellow on black, where the screen is built from slanted panels and every figure is a heavy italic number, so today reads like a race result.
    base: dark
    palette:
        black: #0b0b0a, the page and the style sheet
        panel: #161614, cards and the stats block
        panel2: #20201c, empty tracks, fields and the next session strip
        line: #3a3a33, rules between rows and track outlines
        ink: #f6f6ef, text, week bars, done plan weeks and the secondary button
        muted: #b0b0a2, labels and units
        volt: #d4ff1a, the run hero, ring fill, top zone, today, current plan week, primary button and focus
        onVolt: #0b0b0a, text on volt and on ink
        voltDim: #7d9410, outlines of the quieter zone bars
        rest: #8a8a7e, the Rest word and dash on empty days
    type:
        Figures and headings use Impact, Haettenschweiler, Franklin Gothic
        Heavy, Arial Black, always italic at 900. Text uses Helvetica Neue,
        Arial, system-ui at 15px and 1.45. The run distance is 176px, run
        stats 56px, card titles 26px caps, chart figures 26 to 30px, labels
        12px caps at 800 tracked 0.14em.
    layout:
        A black top bar with a volt slanted BW tile and Move, three slanted
        tabs with Today filled white, and the date in italic caps on the
        right, ruled below in volt. A full width hero has an 8px volt left
        edge. Its left part is a volt panel cut on a slant holding a black
        Done tag with a check, Today 42 min, Evening run and 8.2 km at
        176px. Its right part lists Time 42 min 16 s, Avg pace 5 min 9 s per
        km and Avg heart rate 152 bpm as big italic figures over rules.
        Below, a twelve column grid. Rings takes seven columns with three
        rows, each a caps label, a slanted volt track with a white end tick
        at the goal, and the value over the goal with an open square and the
        amount to go. Heart zones takes five columns as slanted columns with
        minutes on top, zone 3 solid volt and the rest outlined, Z numbers
        and names below and a note on the top zone. This week takes seven
        columns as slanted white columns with today in volt, rest days as a
        grey dash and the word Rest, day names and dates below and the total
        of 23.7 km in the title. A right column stacks Sleep with 7 h 12 m
        in big italic, a slanted deep sleep bar at 22 percent and a key,
        then the Half marathon plan with Week 6 of 12 in volt, twelve
        slanted segments with five white, one volt and six empty, and a next
        strip reading Long run 14 km tomorrow with View plan. Below 980px
        everything stacks and the hero panel loses its slant. At 375px the
        distance drops to 120px and ring tracks move under their labels.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between panels, 24px card padding, a 32px page gutter.
    density: Medium low. One giant result, then five panels with a single chart each.
    corners: None. Bars, tags, tracks, swatches and segments are skewed ten degrees instead.
    borders: An 8px volt bar on the hero edge, a short volt slash on top of each card and 2px rules between rows.
    shadows: None. Flat black panels.
    icons:
        Very few. A square check in the Done tag, an open square for rings
        still to close, and a grey dash with Rest for empty days. Today is
        named Today.
    focus: A 3px volt outline offset 3px, a black gap and a 2px white ring outside it. Slanted buttons drop their slant when focused.
    tone: Short caps labels such as Done, To go, Rest, This week and Long run 14 km.
